# A long walk on the real screens, for a boot in its gap phase (D156, D195). Every press is checked against the
# screen: a key pressed twice, or not at all, puts the highlight or the typed text in the wrong place.
# Safe on any cabinet with no makers: it plays starter carts and types a name it never keeps.
# Takes about a minute a round: `repeat` sets how long it runs.
wait shelf
repeat 40
home
press down
expect-sel 1
press down
expect-sel 2
press down
expect-sel 3
press up
expect-sel 2
press up
expect-sel 1
press up
expect-sel 0
# Typing, read back from the screen.
press a
wait who
press a
wait say typing
type Abc 123
expect Abc 123
press backspace
press backspace
expect Abc 1
type xy
expect Abc 1xy
shot typed
press esc
sleep 300
press esc
sleep 300
press esc
sleep 300
wait shelf
# A hold on a game in play: how far it moved is on the screen.
home
press down
expect-sel 1
press a
wait play
sleep 1200
press a
sleep 800
shot before-hold
hold left 500
shot after-hold
press esc
sleep 800
press esc
sleep 500
wait shelf
sleep 2000
end
